Parameterise the donor in theta, for G4 (M6a/M6b).
=================================================

Apply ONLY in the disposable clone, ONLY for the mutation test:

    cd /home/user/donor-smoke
    git apply marketing_experimentation/repro/recast/theta-mutation.patch

Never in the reference clone, and never before M5b. The golden replay joins
on `effect_label`, so it must run against the unpatched donor.

This is a diff, not vendored source (D5: the donor has no licence). It is
recorded here because the mutation it enables is part of the method, and a
mutation nobody can reproduce is not evidence.

VERIFIED, not illustrative
--------------------------
An earlier version of this file sketched the plot hunks in prose and would
not have applied. This diff was generated by editing a scratch clone and
taking `git diff`, and it is checked:

    git apply --check          clean against a pristine clone at 5133d37
    python -m py_compile       both plot files compile after applying
    Rscript parse()            generate_panels.R parses, 55 expressions
    theta_label()              0 -> null, 0.075 -> effect, 0.02 -> eff_p020,
                               -0.05 -> eff_m050, 0.15 -> eff_p150

WHY IT IS A STRICT SUPERSET
---------------------------
Run with no new flags, the patched generator produces byte-identical output:
theta 0.0 still labels "null", 0.075 still labels "effect". Only a theta
outside that pair gets a new label. So the patch cannot invalidate the
golden replay even if applied by accident -- it can only add.

WHAT EACH HUNK IS FOR, AGAINST THE SIX G4 CRITERIA
--------------------------------------------------
1. generate_panels.R, --effect_sizes flag          -> criterion 1
2. generate_panels.R, magnitude-bearing labels     -> the structural defect:
     effect_labels are directory names, so a second theta silently
     overwrites the first. Blocking for the atlas at M7.
     Resolution is one part in a thousand; a collision is an error, not a
     silent share.
3. analysis/plot_forest.py                         -> criterion 5 (D7)
     true_values / col_titles derived from the data's own true_att_pct,
     the same quantity the metrics layer already trusts, so the figure and
     the table can no longer disagree about what the truth was.
4. analysis/plot_ci_gallery.py                     -> criterion 5 (D7)
     TRUE_ATT set from the loaded results rather than a module constant.
     AND a third coupling found while writing this: load_results() filtered
     on `effect_label == "effect"` -- a literal label, which returns nothing
     once labels carry magnitude. Now filters on effect_pct != 0, which is
     label-independent.

Criteria 2, 4 and 6 need no patch -- see docs/donor-repro.md 5a.

